# Read one of your own Cloud Storage buckets.
# - storage.googleapis.com serves every tenant's bucket under its own first path segment. Allowing
#   the whole host would allow every public bucket on it, so the tree keeps the reach to this one
#   bucket.
# - The line grants reads only. The proxy refuses and logs a request outside the tree, or one
#   spelled outside a rule path's canonical form (doc/egress-proxy.md, "The rule file").
# - A signed upload URL for the bucket still fails here: the proxy refuses a PUT where no line
#   grants it.
# - What travels in an allowed GET's suffix and query is not bounded (SECURITY.md, "Exfiltration
#   through allowed network traffic").
allow https://storage.googleapis.com/my-bucket/ read
